{
  "statement": "The safety and reliability of the bookkeeping system are paramount to prevent data loss, maintain integrity, and ensure fault tolerance. SAF-01 ensures accurate transaction recording to avoid corruption, while SAF-02 enforces double-entry principles to uphold accuracy. SAF-03's audit trail is crucial for accountability and recovery. SAF-04 addresses error handling during transactions, and SAF-05 ensures users can access critical functions during outages. SAF-06 validates currency conversions to prevent discrepancies, and SAF-07 mandates regular data backups. These requirements collectively support a reliable system that safeguards financial data.",
